<figure class="flex flex-col gap-4 border-2 border-ink p-4 sm:p-6">
  <p class="font-bold">The one kilogram of dry matter never changes.</p>
  <svg
    viewBox="0 0 300 198"
    class="w-full max-w-sm"
    role="img"
    aria-labelledby="potato-title potato-desc"
  >
    <title id="potato-title">One hundred kilograms of potatoes drying to fifty kilograms</title>
    <desc id="potato-desc">
      Before drying: 99 kilograms water and 1 kilogram dry matter. After drying: 49 kilograms
      water and the same 1 kilogram dry matter. The total halves to 50 kilograms.
    </desc>
    <g fill="currentColor" font-size="17" font-weight="bold">
      <text x="10" y="22">
        Before: 100 kg
      </text>
      <text x="10" y="122">
        After: 50 kg
      </text>
    </g>
    <rect x="10" y="32" width="277.2" height="30" fill="#387a91" />
    <rect x="287.2" y="32" width="2.8" height="30" fill="#bd4b37" />
    <rect x="10" y="132" width="137.2" height="30" fill="#387a91" />
    <rect x="147.2" y="132" width="2.8" height="30" fill="#bd4b37" />
    <g fill="currentColor" font-size="16">
      <text x="10" y="84">
        99 kg water + 1 kg dry
      </text>
      <text x="10" y="184">
        49 kg water + 1 kg dry
      </text>
    </g>
  </svg>
  <figcaption class="text-base leading-normal">
    The dry portion is fixed at 1 kg. Initially that is 1% of 100 kg. Once it is 2% of the
    total, the total must be 1 ÷ 0.02 = <strong>50 kg</strong>. The thin red end cap is the same
    1 kg in both bars, drawn to scale.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
